Staged, NOT applied. Apply these three files over host/ only when no run is in progress, then delete
this marker:

    cp host/staged/{coolgate.sh,tpu-run.sh,local-run.sh,quality-compare.sh} host/ && rm host/staged/APPLY-PENDING

Why they are staged rather than edited in place: a 24-prompt run was mid-flight when the defect was
found, and quality-compare.sh invokes the runners fresh for every row. Editing them would have put
rows 1-7 under one configuration and rows 8-24 under another, inside one result set.

What they change, and nothing else:
  coolgate.sh       NEW, and SOURCED by both runners so they cannot drift apart again. The gate
                    local-run.sh already had FAILED OPEN: it looped 90 times and then measured anyway
                    whatever it had found. Driven with a fake device at Thermal Status 3 and
                    scaling_max 1000 against cpuinfo_max 2000 it printed the bad reading, launched the
                    run and exited 0. It also never checked the reads, so a failed transport, an empty
                    string or a non-numeric frequency all just looped and fell through. The new one
                    refuses (exit 4) unless the phone is verifiably cool and uncapped, and the only way
                    past is NOCOOL=1, which is printed, recorded in BUILD and folded into the key.
  tpu-run.sh        sources the gate. It had none at all, and quality-compare.sh runs the TPU arm
                    first, so the CPU arm was handed a cool uncapped phone and the masked arm was not.
  local-run.sh      passes --ei mem ${MEM:-8192}. It passed none, and mode local defaults mem to 7168
                    (Main.java), so the two arms ran VMs a gigabyte apart in page cache while
                    tpu-run.sh asked for 8192.
  quality-compare.sh hands the SAME MEM and NOCOOL to both arms, defaults MEM to 8192, and -- the part
                    that matters for applying this at all -- puts the controlled settings (mem, token
                    budget, thermal policy) and a digest of the three runner files into every cache key,
                    into BUILD and into the manifest header. Without that, applying this fix into an
                    existing OUT would find every row "cached" and report logs made by the UNMATCHED
                    runners as a matched run.

Enforced by three suites, against this directory while the marker exists and against host/ once it is
gone: runners-matched-test.sh (the arms gate and size identically), coolgate-test.sh (the REAL runners
against a fake hot/capped/unreadable device -- string-presence checks passed the fail-open gate, so
these assert on exit status and on whether the run was ever launched), and key-binding-test.sh
(changing mem, budget, policy or a runner re-runs the row instead of serving the old one).
